{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1110612-so-here-we-go","id":1110612,"title":"So, here we go...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-02T11:55:38-07:00","id":1110612,"title":"So, here we go...","content":"Hi!<br /> <br /> I'm mostly a Mage player by inclination, but recently I felt compelled to get back into Vampire, and I feel pretty good about Requiem as opposed to Masquerade. So even though I've been around the WW/Onyx Path scene for awhile, I'm kind of a newb when it comes to Requiem. I'm sticking to Second Edition, because it seems to be friendlier to the type of monster it portrays while still holding out hope for cross-compatibility. <br /> <br /> I've got the core Second Edition rulebook and A Thousand Years of Night. What are some of the older 1e corebooks I could get the most use out of until the second edition supplements come out for the newest Vampire?<br /> <br /> (BTW, don't talk to me about nuWW's Vampire; I've seen enough so far to not bother pursuing it. It's not for me, and that's okay.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2176-spectaculartentacular","name":"SpectacularTentacular","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2176_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T12:07:00-07:00","id":1110616,"title":"","content":"Clanbooks. Lots of inspiration for the clans, and very light on mechanics. I like Blasphemies &amp; Sacrements, it ports well and makes blood sorcery a lot more like Mage's magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a hre